<p>US prosecutors are investigating whether Colombian President Gustavo Petro had links to drug traffickers, according to reports cited by multiple outlets. The US Drug Enforcement Administration has also designated him a &quot;priority target,&quot; a step Boston.com said is reserved for suspects believed to have a significant impact on the drug trade. Petro has denied any ties to traffickers. The reports add new strain to already tense US-Colombia relations during President Trump&#x27;s second term, turning a sensitive bilateral relationship into a legal and diplomatic flashpoint. The case stands out because it involves a sitting head of state in one of Washington&#x27;s closest partners in Latin America. Still, the articles provided do not report charges, publicly released evidence, or any formal US court action against Petro so far.</p><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Two prosecutors: Al Jazeera said two US prosecutors opened probes into possible drug-trafficking links involving Petro.</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/us-prosecutors-investigate-whether-colombian-president-petro-had-ties-to-drug-traffickers-reports/a-76461891'>US prosecutors investigate whether Colombian President Petro had ties to drug traffickers — reports</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.boston.com/news/crime/2026/03/20/dea-names-colombian-president-priority-target-as-us-prosecutors-probe-ties-to-drug-traffickers/'>DEA names Colombian president ‘priority target’ as US prosecutors probe ties to drug traffickers</a> - boston.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/20/colombias-president-gustavo-petro-under-investigation-in-us-for-drug-ties'>Colombia’s President Gustavo Petro under investigation in US for drug ties</a> - aljazeera.com</li></ul>